<!-- core:start -->
Plan documents are the working record of an agent's implementation session.
They live in `agents/plans/` in the repository they belong to.

## Filename

Every plan document is named:

```
YYYYMMDD-NN-<kebab-slug>-<id8>.plan.md
```

- `YYYYMMDD` is the plan's `Date:` field. The two must agree: if you change one,
  change the other.
- `NN` is a two-digit sequence number within that date, starting at `01`, in
  order of authorship. A new plan takes the highest number already used for its
  date and adds one.
- `<kebab-slug>` is the plan's `# Plan:` title, lowercased, with spaces turned
  into hyphens and other punctuation removed. Write `AGENTS.md` as `agents`, and
  keep digits as they are (`sha256`).
- `<id8>` is the first eight hexadecimal characters of the plan's UUID. Line 1
  of the document is `<!-- <uuid> -->`. A new plan mints a UUID version 4 and
  uses its first eight characters.

Two examples:

```
agents/plans/20261114-01-reserve-the-reservation-window-5d860648.plan.md
agents/plans/20261011-03-separate-compute-query-timings-932a86ec.plan.md
```

## Structure

A plan document has, in this order:

1. the UUID comment on line 1, `<!-- <uuid> -->`;
2. the `todos` and `isProject` YAML frontmatter;
3. `# Plan: <title>`;
4. the header fields — `Date:` and `Scope:`, plus `Issue:`, `Parent:`, `Branch:`
   and `Result:` where they apply;
5. the plan body;
6. `## Status`;
7. `## AIMetrics`, as the last section.

A plan document carries no `<meta:header>` licence block. Its first content is
the UUID comment and the frontmatter, so a licence header would push the
frontmatter out of place.

## Status

Every plan ends with a `## Status` section:

```markdown
## Status

status: implemented
details: Implemented in commit [`941e9504`](https://github.com/uksrc/Calycopis-broker/commit/941e9504)
  and merged as [PR #202](https://github.com/uksrc/Calycopis-broker/pull/202).
```

`status` is one of:

| Value | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pending` | Planned and approved, nothing implemented yet. |
| `in-progress` | Implementation started, not committed yet. |
| `implemented` | Complete, verified and committed; the details link the commit and the pull request. |
| `on-hold` | Started or approved, then paused; the details say why and what would restart it. |
| `rejected` | Superseded or abandoned; the details link the replacement. |

The details text names the commit(s) and the pull request, and lists any plan
item that is still open. The `todos:` frontmatter is a historical record of the
session and is not rewritten afterwards; the `## Status` section is what answers
"is this plan done", so it has to be kept current.

## AI metrics

Every plan ends with a `## AIMetrics` section, after `## Status`:

````markdown
## AIMetrics

```text
AIMetrics: [
    {
    "timestamp": "<ISO 8601 date and time of the change>",
    "name": "<agent/tool name>",
    "version": "<agent/tool version>",
    "model": "<model identifier>",
    "contribution": {
      "value": <percentage>,
      "units": "%"
      }
    }
  ]
```
````

This is the same fenced block that a GitHub issue or pull request body carries,
because a plan is an authored document and has no single comment header to put
the block in. The block goes at the end of the document, not the top, so that it
is visible when the plan is rendered.

- One entry per change, appended in order; do not remove or rewrite existing
  entries.
- `timestamp` for a change made in one pass, or `interval` covering the edits
  when a change was made in several.
- `contribution.value` is `100` for a plan written in full, and an estimate of
  the percentage of the document's lines changed for a later edit.
- Where a plan predates this rule and only the date of its authorship is known,
  record `"timestamp": "<date>T00:00:00"`.
- A plan edited later gets a new entry and a refreshed `## Status`.
<!-- core:end -->

<!-- local:start -->
The plans written between 2026-05 and 2026-11 were renamed into this convention
for issues #190, #191 and #192. The Cursor-era plans keep the id that Cursor
gave them in its own `cursor/plans` file name, and take their date from the note
that records the plan being saved.

`AGENTS.md` summarises this rule under **Coding rules**. Historical notes under
`notes/` still refer to the plans by their old names and are left as they were:
a note is a record, and is not rewritten to match a later rename.
<!-- local:end -->
